    "summary": "Soaring second set with Foolish Heart, Standing On The Moon & Mighty Quinn",
    "blurb": "The rain‑soaked first set is uneven and ghostly, but the second set erupts with a fiery Foolish Heart, an epic Standing On The Moon, and a triumphant Mighty Quinn finale. Jerry’s tone recovers after a shaky start while Vince’s keyboards sparkle on Samba In The Rain. Overall the band delivers a memorable night despite the downpour.",
    "review": "On July 29, 1994 at Buckeye Lake Music Center the Dead fought through a literal storm to give fans a night that many still call the “Rain Show.” The opening number “Rain” set a drenched tone for a first set that reviewers describe as sluggish and even \"ghostly\" in Garcia’s playing. Yet the band kept the energy moving, slipping into classics like “Althea,” “Eternity,” and a tentative “Deal” before the clouds finally cleared.\n\nWhen the second set kicked off with “Foolish Heart,” the atmosphere shifted dramatically. Jerry found his footing, delivering soaring solos that built into a monumental “Standing On The Moon.” Vince Welnick’s keyboards lit up the new “Samba In The Rain,” and the rhythm section of Bill and Mickey answered the thunder with punchy, energetic drumming. The night culminated in an exuberant encore – “The Mighty Quinn (Quinn The Eskimo)” – leaving the crowd drenched but elated. Despite the weather‑induced challenges, the performance’s high points make this show a standout entry in the ’94 catalog.",
